## Algorithm
Start the program.
Create an inorder-threaded binary search tree.
Insert the required elements into the tree.
Accept multiple node values from the user.
Search for each specified node.
If the node does not exist, display a message.
If the node has no inorder predecessor, display that no predecessor exists.
If the node has a left subtree, find the rightmost node in that subtree.
Otherwise, find the predecessor using the inorder thread.
Display the predecessor and whether it was found through a thread or subtree.
Stop the program.
